<SddCritic keywords="critic, orchestrator, spec-review, task-review, blind-spot, multi-round, reconcile, surgical-edit, sdd-critic" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Autonomous critique loop for one SDD review-set. I am the ORCHESTRATOR and sole owner of its
    edit/re-dispatch loop: each round dispatches one isolated read-only sensor, evaluates findings in
    project context, reconciles introduced entities via `orient`, edits only the manifest-derived
    write-set, and re-dispatches after edits. Five rounds are automatic; crossing each active cap needs
    an operator decision. One primary keeps the shared `## Critic Rounds` until readiness; secondary
    members never duplicate it. Apply every `MECHANICAL` edit
    directly; the round checkpoint asks only about unresolved `GOAL` findings
    (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). Severity never creates a confirm-after-fix Ask. The sensor only reports;
    only the operator downgrades a `GOAL` tag.

    A separate skill (`/sdd-critic`). Input — a spec / task / bounded bundle target. Output — the reviewed bundle
    + the final verdict.
  </Mission>

