  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_ARTIFACT` | The target spec / task does not exist |
    | `H_PARENT_SPEC_MISSING` | A task's parent spec is missing — cannot critique a task without its spec |
    | `H_DISPATCH_FAILED` | The sensor subagent failed to dispatch twice — surface to the operator, do not loop silently |
    | `H_CRITIC_NOT_READY` | `npx gennady sdd-check --review-ready <bundle-path>` fails while evidence still exists — do not finalize or remove it |
    | `H_CRITIC_PUBLICATION_INVALID` | `npx gennady sdd-check --review-publication <primary> [secondary...]` cannot derive one exact role-validated publication-set from the critic's spec-only write-set plus bounded durable outputs — do not remove scratch or publish |
    | `H_GOAL_BLOCKED` | `GOAL` findings block the round and the operator is unavailable to answer — stop, report the pending question block |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_RESOLVE">
      <Goal>Resolve the target.</Goal>
      <Action>Resolve one canonical ordered review-set, its one primary artifact, and the non-empty write-set derived by `sdd-check --review-state` from valid `CHANGE_MANIFEST` sections. Spec review is scope-local: a decomposed product/library scope is primary with ALL its declared module specs; cross-scope neighbours are bounded context, never members of this history. Infrastructure/interface may be standalone. A task batch remains DAG-layered per `AX_TASK_PARALLEL`. Missing → `H_NO_ARTIFACT`. If an existing cycle names another review-set or write-set, start a fresh Round 1 with reason `target-set changed: <reason>` or `write-set changed: <path/reason>`; never continue across either identity.

      Before STEP_1, fold matching `CRITIC_SENSOR_STATE_FORMAT` events against the primary's completed
      `## Critic Rounds`. An unrecorded `sensor-result` is `resumePendingResult`: skip
      STEP_1_DISPATCH through STEP_2C_PERSIST_SENSOR and resume the first incomplete STEP_3 → STEP_3C
      transition. A required disposition that is absent re-presents the Ask from the persisted result;
      an existing disposition is applied without asking again. Neither path redispatches, increments,
      or resets the pending result. Only no pending result may enter STEP_1.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_0B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear the FLOW_VERSION/READINESS preflight gate before dispatching the sensor.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Use `FLOW_VERSION`, `AUTHORING_READY`, `EXECUTION_READY`, and `GATE_QUEUE` from the already-gathered `sdd-state`
        snapshot; do not enter task lifecycle merely to clear this gate. Size the gate to this request's own blast radius
        (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`). The router already applied the shared readiness gate
        before loading this directive; do not repeat or reinterpret it here.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_DISPATCH">
      <Goal>Dispatch the isolated sensor.</Goal>
      <Action>Enter only when STEP_0 found no `resumePendingResult`. Immediately before EVERY dispatch, run exact reviewState ToolCall below; retain its Target-set, Write-set, and Changed-state in this round. The sensor always reads the full review-set and receives the exact current session `glossary:` list as read-only input. Round 1 is fresh. For a later round over the SAME review-set/write-set, continue that SAME worker/session when supported, sending the changed-set plus explicit confirmation that the full target-set is unchanged and the write-set is unchanged. Record `Dispatch: continued`. A fresh fallback is allowed only when continuation is unsupported, the session was lost, or the sensor failed; send the full review-set and record `fresh — continuation unavailable: <reason>`, `fresh — session lost: <reason>`, or `fresh — session failed: <reason>`. Never invoke a nested agent CLI to simulate continuation. Use a worker-tier model (`AX_CRITIC_MODEL_TIER`); every handoff names primary, round, protocol, sets, Changed-state, and saved glossary. Emit one `ORCHESTRATOR_PROGRESS_FORMAT` line. <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="reviewState">npx gennady sdd-check --review-state <primary> [secondary...]</ToolCall> Inputs <primary>, [secondary...]: <primary>=canonical primary resolved in STEP_0; [secondary...]=same ordered remaining review-set from STEP_0. Use reviewState.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_EVALUATE">
      <Goal>Weigh findings against full project context.</Goal>
      <Action>Split by addressee (`AX_FINDING_ADDRESSEE`): `MECHANICAL` — accept by default (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`); `GOAL` — queue for STEP_3B (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). Parse the sensor's final `GlossarySuggestions` field per `SESSION_FILE_FORMAT`; deduplicate it against the saved glossary and carry genuinely new/conflicting items to the next existing operator checkpoint, never a glossary-only Ask. A finding that requires changing a read-only review-set member cannot enter this cycle's edit set: either route it as a blocker to that artifact's authoring owner, or promote the member by adding a valid manifest and RESTART with `write-set changed: <path/reason>`. Never edit it silently. A rejection cites a specific resolving file/section (`AX_REJECTION_REASON`). Sensor confusion the full context resolves = artifact bug (`AX_CONFUSION_BUG`); project ambiguity = `GOAL`. Carry severity (`AX_SEVERITY`); weakening a quality gate is always `GOAL`.

      Convergence brake from round 3 on: a NEW finding (not already carried in a prior `## Critic Rounds` entry) advances to STEP_3 / STEP_3B only if `CRITICAL`, or a regression — a defect a prior round's own edit introduced. A new `MINOR` / `MAJOR` finding that is neither stays out of this cycle's edit set — record it in this round's entry under `Out of cycle:` and carry it into the STEP_5 report as its own list, never silently dropped (AUTHORING.md §9 — a stop needs a named outlet, not a bare refusal).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_RECONCILE">
      <Goal>Walk the graph from the artifact to the portal; reconcile every entity the WHOLE artifact introduces, not only this round's findings. (mechanical → tool)</Goal>
      <Action>Run exact orientation ToolCall below once for EACH artifact in the bounded target-set — one hop from that artifact to its portal, declared-dependency neighbours, and consumers; this is the ORCHESTRATOR's own step, on full project context, not a widening of the sensor's bounded read (`AX_ISOLATION_SIGNAL` still governs STEP_1_DISPATCH). The sweep is proactive over EVERY entity/contract/mechanism the bundle introduces, never narrowed to only the entities this round's findings happen to name — a duplicate the sensor never flagged is still a duplicate. For each: reuse > extend > justify > escalate (`AX_REUSE_FIRST`); "justify" requires the specific neighbour invariant/requirement ID the existing mechanism could not satisfy, recorded as its own Decision Log entry (`AX_PARALLEL_MECHANISM_REQUIRES_JUSTIFICATION`, `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`). Two outcomes route to `GOAL`, never a silent `MECHANICAL` fix: (1) the artifact duplicates a mechanism the `sdd-orient` extract already names on a neighbour, (2) the artifact's introduced entity conflicts with a neighbour requirement the extract surfaces. Do not let the critique invent a duplicate of an existing entity. <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="orientation">npx gennady sdd-orient <artifact-path></ToolCall> Inputs <artifact-path>: <artifact-path>=each literal Target-set member returned by STEP_1, one separate call per member. Use orientation.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2C_PERSIST_SENSOR">
      <Goal>Make the returned sensor result and cumulative count durable before any decision or edit.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Set `resultCount` to the next canonical Round number and append the exact `sensor-result`
        event through `CRITIC_SENSOR_STATE_FORMAT`; require criticEvent success. This transition
        occurs after addressee/reconcile classification but BEFORE STEP_3, every GOAL/cap Ask,
        CLEAN/proceed, or another dispatch. On resume, consume a matching pending event rather than
        dispatching the sensor again; never increment a recorded result twice.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="criticSensorEvent">npx gennady sdd-session log --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-critic-event.json</ToolCall> Payload: exact sensor-result event. Use criticSensorEvent before STEP_3.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_EDIT">
      <Goal>Apply the round's `MECHANICAL` edits.</Goal>
      <Action>Edit only write-set members and only what a finding requires (`AX_SURGICAL`); I apply edits — the sensor never does (`AX_OWNER`). Apply every `MECHANICAL` finding directly (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`) regardless of severity; severity does not create an extra confirmation. Leave `GOAL` sections untouched until the operator answers. Record the round's edits once at STEP_3C.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3B_ROUND_CHECKPOINT">
      <Goal>One batch Ask per round for every operator-owned item (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Resolve every `GOAL` finding against accepted operator decisions and the Decision Log first.
        Auto-resolution is allowed only when the same answer was previously accepted by the operator,
        still applies with unchanged consequences, and is cited by its Decision Log id or exact prior
        operator-decision record. Every other `GOAL` is new — regardless of low risk, an apparent
        default, or preserved product intent — and enters the batch before any related edit. Its
        question names the consequence that makes it new or reopens it. Build ONE
        `AskUserQuestion` batch (`QUESTION_FORMAT` batching rule — independent questions ride
        together) carrying every remaining new `GOAL` fork from STEP_2 or STEP_2B as its own question,
        including any orchestrator disagreement with a sensor's `GOAL` tag («critic tagged GOAL, I read
        this as mechanical because …») — the tag stands until this answer says otherwise. A
        `CRITICAL` / `MAJOR` mechanical finding never creates a separate confirm-after-edit Ask. When
        no unresolved `GOAL` exists →
        skip the Ask, go straight to STEP_3C (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`). WAIT for the answer
        before touching any `GOAL`-tagged section. Before applying an answer, append its separate
        immutable `goal-disposition` event for this `resultCount` and require criticEvent success.
        Apply `GOAL` edits exactly as answered, and any
        correction the operator makes to a confirmed fix — recorded together at STEP_3C, not here.
        When this checkpoint or `H_GOAL_BLOCKED` waits for the operator, return
        `TerminalDecision: pause` and preserve the SDD session; an unresolved Ask is never
        completion. When the answered `GOAL` finding weakened or removed a quality gate, additionally write the
        operator's decision as its own Decision Log entry (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). Any accepted glossary
        item sharing this checkpoint is persisted with the inherited router glossaryUpdate before reuse. Operator unreachable
        while `GOAL` findings block → `H_GOAL_BLOCKED`.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="criticGoalDispositionEvent">npx gennady sdd-session log --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-critic-event.json</ToolCall> Payload: exact goal-disposition event. Use criticGoalDispositionEvent before applying the answer.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3B2_CAP_DECISION">
      <Goal>At the active automatic cap, obtain the operator's explicit disposition before another dispatch (`AX_CAP_5`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Rounds before the active cap skip this step. At Round 5 — and at every operator-raised cap — Ask
        regardless of sensor verdict. If `Changes: none`, offer exactly: (a) operator CLEAN; (b) continue
        through an explicitly named higher cap `CONTINUE THROUGH ROUND <N>`; (c) correct target/approach
        and `RESTART: <reason>`. If this round edited any write-set member, CLEAN is unavailable because
        those bytes have not had a subsequent sensor pass; offer only CONTINUE or RESTART. Before
        applying the exact answer, append its separate immutable `cap-disposition` event for this
        `resultCount` and require criticEvent success. CLEAN keeps
        the sensor verdict honest and permits readiness without another dispatch; CONTINUE permits only rounds through the new cap;
        RESTART ends this cycle, applies the correction, recomputes review-state, and starts a fresh Round 1.
        While this cap decision is unanswered, return `TerminalDecision: pause` and preserve the
        session. The sensor cannot authorize a sixth round. Never rewrite its verdict into
        `OPERATOR_ACCEPTED`.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="criticCapDispositionEvent">npx gennady sdd-session log --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-critic-event.json</ToolCall> Payload: exact cap-disposition event. Use criticCapDispositionEvent before applying the answer.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3C_RECORD_ROUND">
      <Goal>Append this round's memory to the artifact (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Append ONE entry to `## Critic Rounds` in the one primary artifact only — create the section at
        the end of that artifact on Round 1; secondary target artifacts never receive a copy. Never
        rewrite a prior entry; this block is append-only:

        ```
        ### Round <N> — <YYYY-MM-DD>
        - Verdict: <CLEAN|NEEDS_WORK|CRITICAL>
        - Target-set: <canonical sorted bundle paths joined by " | ">
        - Write-set: <canonical sorted writable paths joined by " | ">
        - Changed-state: <exact sha256 value from STEP_1 reviewState.Changed-state>
        - Dispatch: <fresh — initial target-set | continued | fresh — target-set/write-set changed: reason | fresh — continuation unavailable/session lost/session failed: reason>
        - Accepted: <count> — <list>
        - Rejected: <count> — "<finding>" → <reason>
        - Reconcile: <entity → REUSE <target> | EXTEND <target> | JUSTIFY <rationale> | ESCALATE>
        - Changes: <none | concrete edited members>
        - Out of cycle: <new MINOR/MAJOR findings the round-3+ brake deferred, or "none">
        - Operator-decision: <CLEAN|CONTINUE THROUGH ROUND N|RESTART: reason> # only when STEP_3B2 asked
        ```

        `Accepted` covers both the `MECHANICAL` edits applied at STEP_3 and the `GOAL` edits applied at
        STEP_3B after the operator's answer. `Rejected` carries the exact reason per `AX_REJECTION_REASON`
        — a later round, or a later session picking this up fresh, reads this entry before re-raising the
        same ground. Even on a CLEAN round this entry is appended before STEP_5 runs readiness; the block
        must still exist when the command validates it (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`).
        After this canonical entry is durable, append `round-recorded` through
        `CRITIC_SENSOR_STATE_FORMAT`. A context resume consumes the pending sensor/disposition events
        and finishes this step without redispatching or incrementing the result.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="criticRoundRecordedEvent">npx gennady sdd-session log --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-critic-event.json</ToolCall> Payload: exact round-recorded event. Use criticRoundRecordedEvent before STEP_4.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_DECIDE">
      <Goal>Loop or stop.</Goal>
      <Action>Before the active cap: CLEAN with `Changes: none` → STEP_5; any edits → another dispatch (`AX_RE_DISPATCH`) whose STEP_1 `reviewState.Changed-state` must differ; zero edits with a non-clean verdict → stop not-ready and never dispatch another round (`AX_STOP_NO_EDITS`). At the cap: operator CLEAN is valid only with `Changes: none` and goes to STEP_5 without another dispatch; CONTINUE raises the cap and continues; RESTART returns to STEP_0 as a fresh cycle. No automatic dispatch crosses the cap (`AX_CAP_5`).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Finalize.</Goal>
      <Action>While the primary's `## Critic Rounds` still exists, run exactly projectFeasibility ToolCall below before reviewReadiness. A project-feasibility finding means the reviewed specs have inconsistent declared rows or artifact ownership: return it to the owning scope/infra external-dependencies audit and do not finalize a scope-local CLEAN. A GREEN result is structural evidence only; this critic still owns the semantic judgement that the specs are jointly executable. Then run exactly reviewReadiness ToolCall below. Failure → `H_CRITIC_NOT_READY`. Then run exact reviewPublication ToolCall below with the same ordered spec arguments used by review-state; failure → `H_CRITIC_PUBLICATION_INVALID`. Retain and return its literal `target-set`, spec-only `write-set`, role-bearing JSON `publication-set`, and `publication-state`; auxiliary publication members never enter critic ownership. Keep `## Critic Rounds` intact: the review lifecycle removes it only after semantic finalization, the final delta-only operator disposition, and the last publication recheck. Report the literal final sensor verdict (CLEAN | NEEDS_WORK | CRITICAL), the separate operator decision when present, and a one-line-per-round summary, plus merged `Out of cycle` findings and the retained publication output. The verdict MUST be the literal verdict of the LAST sensor dispatch actually run (`AX_RE_DISPATCH`), never a paraphrase and never replaced by operator CLEAN. A structural problem the critique cannot resolve surgically → escalate, do not loop.

      When review-lifecycle dispatched this critic, return `TerminalDecision: continue` with the saved
      publication output and retained scratch to that already-loaded caller; internal review handoff never closes the
      session. For a forced direct `critic` entry, render the terminal menu per
      `NEXT_STEP_MENU_FORMAT`: continuing into review-lifecycle returns `continue`, pause returns
      `pause`, and only after this step establishes `unfinished chained work: none` may literal
      «Complete / finish» removes scratch only after revalidating the unchanged publication output, then
      returns `TerminalDecision: complete` and runs exact terminal ToolCall below once. The decision source
      is this STEP_5 direct-entry menu, never CLEAN or a successful check. A pause or continuation keeps
      scratch. <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="projectFeasibility">npx gennady sdd-check --project-feasibility</ToolCall> Use projectFeasibility before reviewReadiness.<ToolCall owner="this-step" result="reviewReadiness">npx gennady sdd-check --review-ready <bundle-path></ToolCall> Inputs <bundle-path>: <bundle-path>=primary artifact path resolved in STEP_0 whose Critic Rounds embeds the frozen bundle. Use reviewReadiness.<ToolCall owner="this-step" result="reviewPublication">npx gennady sdd-check --review-publication <primary> [secondary...]</ToolCall> Inputs <primary>, [secondary...]: <primary> and [secondary...]=same ordered spec arguments frozen by STEP_1 review-state. Use reviewPublication.<ToolCall owner="this-step" result="terminal">npx gennady sdd-session close</ToolCall></Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

